// Behavioral fixture — laying down a Go Fish "book" (4 of a kind).
//
// Deterministic deck (10 cards, one suit): Ace x4, King x2, Three x4.
// The `Book` combo is `same Rank and size >= 4`; the combo-source move
// prompts over the whole hand and validates the selection. The player
// selects the four Aces -> valid, laid down. (A 2+2 split would also pass
// the filter — a documented D-16 simplification; a 3+1 split is rejected.)
player P1
turnorder (P:P1)
location Hand on P:P1
location Books on table
location Deck on table

combo Book where (same Rank and size >= 4)

card on Deck:
  Rank(Ace, Ace, Ace, Ace, King, King, Three, Three, Three, Three)
    for Suit(Diamonds)

stage Deal for current 1 times {
  deal 10 from Deck private to Hand
}

stage LayBook for current 1 times {
  move Book in Hand of current private to Books
}
